.TH SQL 1 "May 2026" "sql-console 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sql \- A modern SQL console with server-side pagination and export capabilities.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sql
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISQL_STATEMENT\fR]
.br
.B sql profile
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sql
is a CLI client for sql-console-daemon. It provides an interactive REPL or one-shot execution mode for running SQL queries against various database profiles.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " profile"
Specify the database profile name.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Export results to a file (e.g., result.csv).
.TP
.BI \-format " fmt"
Specify export format: csv. Auto-detected from file extension if omitted.
.TP
.BI \-sql_id " id"
Query ID to fetch from cache for pagination.
.TP
.BI \-page " num"
Page number to fetch when using -sql_id.
.TP
.BI \-set-transaction " mode"
Set transaction mode: auto-commit | manual-commit.
.TP
.B \-version
Show version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B profile list
List all saved profiles.
.TP
.B profile add
Add a new database profile.
.TP
.B profile delete
Delete an existing profile.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive REPL:
sql -p my_db
.TP
One-shot execution:
sql -p my_db "SELECT * FROM users"
.TP
Export to CSV:
sql -p my_db -o users.csv "SELECT * FROM users"
.TP
Pagination (Fetch page 2):
sql -p my_db -sql_id abc12345 -page 2
.SH SEE ALSO
sql-console-daemon(8)
.SH AUTHOR
Pollo Lab
